\[ p_s(x) = \sum_{i=0}^{9} a_i \ell_i(x), \]
where $\ell_i(x) = \prod_{\substack{0 \le j \le 9 \\ j \neq i}} \frac{x - j}{i - j}$.

Because of this, we need to compute $p_s(10)$ for each tuple and sum these values over all $s \in S$. Notice that $p_s(10) = \sum_{i=0}^{9} a_i \ell_i(10)$. The expression $\ell_i(10)$ only depends on $i$, so it is the same for all polynomials $p_s(x)$. Specifically, $\ell_i(10) = \prod_{\substack{0 \le j \le 9 \\ j \neq i}} \frac{10 - j}{i - j} = (-1)^{10-i} \binom{10}{i}$. So, $p_s(10) = \sum_{i=0}^{9} a_i (-1)^{10-i} \binom{10}{i}$. We need to sum such values for all polynomials $p_s(x)$, which means we need to sum over all possible tuples $(a_0, a_1, \ldots, a_9)$. This can be simplified using symmetry arguments.

